{
  "configuration_id": "config_051",
  "reason": "Evidence: PCA (pca_n2000) as a unimodal RNA encoder (config_017, acc=0.5907) substantially outperforms scGPT (config_002, acc=0.5305) and all multimodal configurations tested so far (best: config_006, scgpt+ViT-L, acc=0.5420). The best multimodal setup uses ViT-L, avgpool, weighted fusion. However, PCA has never been tested in a multimodal context, leaving a critical uncertainty: does adding image information to the already-strong PCA representation help, or does it dilute the signal? Question: config_051 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) directly swaps the RNA encoder in the best multimodal configuration (config_006) while holding image encoder, aggregation, and fusion constant. This isolates the RNA encoder effect in the multimodal setting and tests whether the image modality provides complementary information on top of PCA. Why this is the best next experiment: it resolves the single most important open question—whether the search should exploit the strong PCA unimodal result or whether a PCA-based multimodal model can surpass it—using a minimal, controlled change from the best existing multimodal setup. The outcome will directly guide whether subsequent experiments should focus on PCA+image fusion variants or on further improving the PCA unimodal baseline."
}

